+Speed up {func}`~scanpy.pp.harmony_integrate` 6–13× with parallel numba kernels, and add the `seeding`, `stop_rule`, `penalty_combine`, `seeding_lloyd_steps`, `seeding_cells_per_cluster`, `recompute_counts` and `low_memory` parameters.
+For `flavor="harmony2"`, the default seeding is now `"afkmc2"`, and the default stop rule for both flavors is `"reference_record"`; pass `seeding="kmeans", stop_rule="reference"` for the previous behaviour.
+Cells with an all-zero embedding are now left out and returned unchanged {smaller}`T Treis`
